# Comments

For any code comment you write, edit, or review, follow `docs/COMMENTS.md`.
A typical change adds zero.

When writing:

- A comment records something genuinely surprising that a reader could
  not glean from the code in front of them. Before writing one, change
  the code so it is not surprising: a name, a type, a split, a test. Write
  the comment only for what remains.
- A comment longer than the code under it is deleted or moved to `docs/`.
  The one exception is a single block describing a sizeable, novel
  algorithm or protocol whose shape the code cannot show at once.
- Before finishing, delete half of the comments you added. Then reread the
  rest.

When reviewing: a comment finding is that the comment is false, that it
documents a surprise the code should have removed (the finding is the
rename, type, or split, not the comment), or that it documents nothing
surprising (the finding is delete). Never request a comment.
